Setting up the backup for file using version control system

Remote Server
-------------

sudo mkdir -p /home/backups/backup

cd /home/backups/backup

sudo git init --bare

Client Side
-----------

git init (It should be done in the backup directory)

git remote add origin username@host:/path_of_directory

git commit --allow-empty -am "Init"

Remote Server
-------------

Change the ownership (sudo chown -R username:username /home/backups/backup.git

Client side
-----------

git commit -m "Commit Message"

Remote Server
-------------

git log main/master --stat --> Show's the status for the recent commit's

git ls-tree -r main --name-only (show the name's of the backup file's)

Extracting the file's
=====================

sudo mkdir -p /home/backups/extracted_files

cd /home/backups/extracted_files

git --work-tree=/home/backups/extracted_files --git-dir=/home/backups/backup.git checkout -f branch




